{
  "id": "ss.char.hex",
  "name": "Hex",
  "description": "The broodmother: a summoner of the brood in a long violet robe. A deep hood with a chitin crest, violet hair showing at the sides, the mouth set grim; the robe falls to the ankles and is worked with the hive's own cells in a lighter thread — the hexagon it used to be — with a steel clasp at the throat. On the back, carried like a reliquary on a strap, a brood vent: the puckered plate that pushes out grubs, and two grubs riding it already, one over the shoulder and one at the hip, that never stop moving, because a grub does not know it is not at home. In the near hand a chitin staff topped with an empty cell. The arms are the slightest on the roster; Hex does not hit anything itself, it sends things. The dead feelers rise long from the crest. Same dead organ as the rest, worn at the clasp. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
